WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.839
Times have been tough for the Dutton clan
over the first two seasons of Paramount Network's

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:09.940
breakout Western drama Yellowstone, but they've
apparently been even tougher on series headliner

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.060
Kevin Costner.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.300
From the sound of it, Costner has recently
been having some second thoughts about signing

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.280
onto Yellowstone.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.580
The actor recently sat down with Indiewire
to talk about the show's recently-wrapped

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:25.060
second season, and to hear him tell it, he's
not enjoying certain aspects of the modern

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.720
cowboy drama's production.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:31.280
Outside of the rigorous shooting schedule,
Costner's biggest issue with Yellowstone is

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.280
apparently that he often feels left in the
dark in regards to his character's past, and

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.480
where Dutton is headed emotionally from episode
to episode.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.860
Costner told Indiewire:

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.380
"I'm not always privy to [aspects of the character's
arc], no.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.880
Sometimes with [Dutton's] sons or wife or
whatever, that's been really kept in a creative

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.380
ball.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.120
That's a more vulnerable way to go through
life as an actor."

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.440
Given the rash of melodramatic twists and
turns that have accompanied seemingly every

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.870
new episode of Yellowstone over the show's
first two seasons, it's easy to understand

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.239
why Costner might want a little more info
about his character, after all, it would be

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:09.210
difficult for any actor, even one of Costner's
caliber, to navigate all that madness with

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.620
any kind of emotional honesty.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.360
For Costner in particular, Yellowstone has
proven an even bigger challenge, because he's

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.780
spent the bulk of his decades-long career
starring in feature films, which allow actors

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.251
to study the entirety of their self-contained
storylines, and plot out their characters'

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:25.570
arcs from start to finish.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:30.229
Hard as it is to believe, Yellowstone is only
the second television series Costner has ever

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:35.140
starred in, with the first being the limited,
three episode run of the History Channel mini-series

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.400
Hatfields &amp; McCoys.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:41.400
In spite of Yellowstone's breakout success,
Costner still hasn't gotten used to the vulnerability

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.210
that comes with not knowing what lies ahead
for his character.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.340
During his interview, Costner bluntly stated:

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.720
"It hasn't been an easy adjustment for me.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.980
I don't like it too much."

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.110
While this may lead fans to believe that Costner
has designs on skedaddling from Yellowstone,

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.710
thankfully, this isn't the case.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.580
"Well ain't that the thing about problems,
Dutton.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.100
No matter how long you’re gone, they'll
be right here when you get back."

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.240
Given the series' impressive viewership numbers,
Costner is enjoying as large an audience as

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:11.459
he has at any point in his storied career;
Yellowstone is one of the most-watched series

00:02:11.459 --> 00:02:15.980
on cable television, and its ratings hit an
all-time high with the season 2 finale.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.340
Though Costner may never quite adjust to the
rigorous shooting schedule and the sometimes

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.840
cloudy narrative of the series, he's still
very much the star of a hit show, and is a

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.300
crucial part of why fans keep coming back
from one week to the next.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:33.160
As it happens, the showrunners are reportedly
mapping out the show's fourth run of episodes

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:37.489
already, and may have as many as seven full
seasons of Yellowstone in the works, and there's

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:40.840
little doubt that they want Costner in the
saddle for as long as he can ride.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:46.730
For proof of that, look no further than the
actor's astonishing $500,000 per episode salary,

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.769
because nothing says "we love you" quite like
a good payday.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:54.530
Seriously, put this into perspective: Yellowstone
ran for nine episodes in its first season,

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.199
and was bumped up to 10 episodes for season
2.

00:02:57.199 --> 00:03:02.650
If the episode order stays at ten, and Yellowstone
does indeed run for a full seven seasons,

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:07.280
it would finish its run with 69 episodes,
which means Costner stands to net a whopping

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.820
$34.5 million for his work on the show.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.460
Of course, given that the role of the duplicitous
Dutton is an exceedingly complex one, it's

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:19.529
unlikely that Costner will get bored with
the gig anytime soon, either, and that can

00:03:19.529 --> 00:03:20.500
only be a good thing.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:24.620
However they do it, though, you can be certain
Yellowstone's creative team will do everything

00:03:24.629 --> 00:03:29.459
in their power to ensure that Kevin Costner
is roping, ranching, and scheming on the small

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.120
screen for the foreseeable future.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:36.180
The series' highly anticipated third season
is expected to premiere on Paramount Network

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.880
in the summer of 2020.

